# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005356> (Rathke's pouch)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "MP:0003817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Wikipedia:Rathke's_pouch") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005356> "A pouch of ectoderm that grows out from the upper surface of the embryonic stomodeum and gives rise to the anterior and intermediate lobes of the pituitary gland[MP]. In embryogenesis, Rathke's pouch is a depression in the roof of the developing mouth in front of the buccopharyngeal membrane. It gives rise to the anterior pituitary (adenohypophysis), a part of the endocrine system[WP].")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002174> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005356> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_7955>)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "http://webs.lander.edu/rsfox/invertebrates/ammocoetes.html") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000008> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005356> "median funnel­-shaped invagination of ectoderm, the nasohypophyseal pouch. It will contribute to the formation of the pituitary gland of the adult lamprey and is homologous to Rathke's pouch and perhaps to Hatschek 's pit (amphioxus).")
